{
  "description": "Cases for the Starter Template's custom lint rules (templates/starter/eslint.config.mjs). Each has a file name (rules apply by path), code, and the message fragments the lint must report, in order; an empty list means clean. orchestrator/test_starter_lint.py runs them. A new or tightened rule adds cases here.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a test reads an application file (named import)",
      "filename": "backend/src/__tests__/x.test.ts",
      "code": "import { readFileSync } from \"node:fs\";\nit(\"x\", () => { expect(readFileSync(\"src/app.ts\", \"utf8\")).toContain(\"x\"); });\n",
      "expect": [
        "source text"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a test reads an application file (member call)",
      "filename": "backend/src/__tests__/x.test.ts",
      "code": "import fs from \"node:fs\";\nit(\"x\", () => { expect(fs.readFileSync(\"src/app.ts\", \"utf8\")).toContain(\"x\"); });\n",
      "expect": [
        "source text"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a test asserts on flags.json",
      "filename": "backend/src/__tests__/x.test.ts",
      "code": "it(\"records the flag\", () => { const entry = load(\"flags.json\"); expect(entry).toEqual({}); });\n",
      "expect": [
        "flags.json"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a test left with .only",
      "filename": "backend/src/__tests__/x.test.ts",
      "code": "it.only(\"x\", () => { expect(1).toBe(1); });\n",
      "expect": [
        ".only"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "a suite left with .only",
      "filename": "backend/src/__tests__/x.test.ts",
